      "precision": "significant_figures",
      "note": "Table 5 of the paper, 6050 A row, prints the refractivity (n-1)10^7 = 2762.65, which is n = 1.000276265. An exact grid point on the table's 50 A step, so nothing is interpolated. Confirmed on the page image at 400 dpi. Cross-checked inside its own row: the table also prints the vacuum correction (n*lambda - lambda) = 1.6714 A at this wavelength, and 6050 A x 2762.65e-7 = 1.67140 A, so the refractivity and the correction agree to five figures and the digits were read right. Rewriting a printed refractivity as an index is a change of form and not a derivation. The probable error is 3.1 in (n-1)10^7, so the last two decimals shown sit inside the noise; they are kept as printed rather than rounded."
    }
  ],
  "validity": {
